/*  FUNCTION NAME:      REPLACEARRAY
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Stamps a scalar, vector, or 2-D block into a host array at an anchor, preserving the host's shape (or growing it in expand mode).*/
/*  RETURNS:            array: the host array with the block stamped in at the anchor (grown in expand mode)
    PARAMETERS:
        replace         (Required) Host array to write into.
        with            (Required) Scalar, vector, or 2-D block to stamp in. Blank cells read as 0 (INDEX quirk).
        at              (Optional) Anchor (top-left) as a single scalar: an A1 text address like "B2" or an encoded pos (row*_mult+col, e.g. from POSAT). Default = origin (top-left).
        overflow        (Optional) Edge handling when the block runs past the host: (0) clip [default], (1) error, (2) expand, (3) wrap.
        origin          (Optional) Top-left anchor as a workbook reference — a single cell or a range (a range's top-left is used). Defaults to the host's own top-left — inferred for a reference, (1,1) for an array.
    EXAMPLE:            =REPLACEARRAY({1,2,3;4,5,6;7,8,9}, {0,0;0,0}, "B2") -> {1,2,3;4,0,0;7,0,0}
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-06-13  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-06-16  Claude      Single-scalar anchor: at accepts an A1 address or an encoded pos (drop the col param); add explicit origin per the position convention
                        2026-06-16  Claude      origin is a workbook reference only (single cell or range; top-left used) — no text-address form, and no ISTEXT test that lifted on a 2-D range
                        2026-11-08  Claude      Hot-loop speed: build only the chosen mode, a native IF mask for one cell, one TOPOS for at, result not bound to a name (#412)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
REPLACEARRAY = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [replace],
    [with],
    [at],
    [overflow],
    [origin],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        nRows, ROWS(replace),
        nCols, COLUMNS(replace),
        wRows, ROWS(with),
        wCols, COLUMNS(with),
        oPos, IF(ISOMITTED(origin),
                 IF(ISREF(replace), MIN(ROW(replace)) * _mult + MIN(COLUMN(replace)), _mult + 1),
                 MIN(ROW(origin)) * _mult + MIN(COLUMN(origin))),
        pos, IF(ISOMITTED(at), oPos, IF(ISTEXT(at), TOPOS(at), at)),
        atRow, INT(pos / _mult) - INT(oPos / _mult) + 1,
        atCol, MOD(pos, _mult) - MOD(oPos, _mult) + 1,
        mode, IF(ISOMITTED(overflow), 0, overflow),
        validAnchor, AND(atRow >= 1, atCol >= 1, atRow = INT(atRow), atCol = INT(atCol)),
        rseq, SEQUENCE(nRows),
        cseq, SEQUENCE(, nCols),
        fits, AND(atRow + wRows - 1 <= nRows, atCol + wCols - 1 <= nCols),
    //  The result. Only the chosen mode is built: a LET binding is evaluated on every call, an
    //  IF branch only when taken. The result is not bound to a name: binding a grid costs a copy
        IF(NOT(validAnchor), NA(),
                IF(mode = 2,
                //  Expand: grow the output so the whole block fits; new host cells are blank
                    LET(
                        rE, SEQUENCE(MAX(nRows, atRow + wRows - 1)),
                        cE, SEQUENCE(, MAX(nCols, atCol + wCols - 1)),
                        bRow, rE - atRow + 1,
                        bCol, cE - atCol + 1,
                        IF((bRow >= 1) * (bRow <= wRows) * (bCol >= 1) * (bCol <= wCols),
                           INDEX(with, IF(bRow < 1, 1, IF(bRow > wRows, wRows, bRow)), IF(bCol < 1, 1, IF(bCol > wCols, wCols, bCol))),
                           IF((rE <= nRows) * (cE <= nCols), INDEX(replace, IF(rE > nRows, nRows, rE), IF(cE > nCols, nCols, cE)), ""))),
                IF(mode = 3,
                //  Wrap: indices wrap modulo host dimensions (toroidal)
                    LET(
                        dRow, MOD(rseq - atRow, nRows),
                        dCol, MOD(cseq - atCol, nCols),
                        IF((dRow < wRows) * (dCol < wCols), INDEX(with, IF(dRow < wRows, dRow + 1, 1), IF(dCol < wCols, dCol + 1, 1)), replace)),
                IF((mode = 1) * NOT(fits), NA(),
                //  Clip (and error mode when the block fits). One cell is a native IF mask
                IF(wRows * wCols = 1, IF((rseq = atRow) * (cseq = atCol), with, replace),
                    LET(
                        sRow, rseq - atRow + 1,
                        sCol, cseq - atCol + 1,
                        IF((sRow >= 1) * (sRow <= wRows) * (sCol >= 1) * (sCol <= wCols),
                           INDEX(with, IF(sRow < 1, 1, IF(sRow > wRows, wRows, sRow)), IF(sCol < 1, 1, IF(sCol > wCols, wCols, sCol))),
                           replace)))))))
)
);
